            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.265,
            0.794,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The names of temperature scales—Celsius scale Fahrenheit scale and Kelvin scale—start with a canital letter. For the units for temperature, degree Celsius and degree Fahrenheit, the word degree starts with a lower-case letter while Celsius and Fahrenheit start with a capital letter. The unit kelvin starts with a lower-case letter. The symbols of all units (°c °℉ k) are capital letters. Note that degree sign (°) is not written with K A full stop is not written after the symbol, except at the end of a sentence While writing the temperature, a space is left between the numher and the unit. For temperatures more than one degree. use the plural of \"degree', that is, 'degrees', while writing the full form of the unit"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.566,
            0.348,
            0.703
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can a clinical thermometer be used for measuring the temperature of "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "boiling water? Or for m",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "eas",
              "styles": [
                "bold",
                "subscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "uring",
              "styles": [
                "bold",
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "the",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " temperature of ice?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.742,
            0.324,
            0.853
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "No, the temperatures of boiling water and ice are outside the range of a clinical thermometer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.418,
            0.544,
            0.806,
            0.625
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How was fever detected before thermometers were developed? Fever affects the pulse rate of a person. This was known even in olden days"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.403,
            0.636,
